Subject: a SETXATTR's form is the request's own, so Shards' owner word sized before INIT was answered is taken (slates A-741)
Why: kiln's macOS microVM g266 drive refused a run's every write EACCES, intermittently: Linux sizes a SETXATTR by the form it holds at the call and holds it until INIT's reply, so Shards' init's owner word comes short on a connection that kept the extended form; slates main e0c06750 (be465b23) reads each request's own form; carried until kiln re-vendors at or past it

